IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `types`
IMPORT `chapter-2-explanations`
IMPORT `chapter-4-exceptions`
IMPORT `chapter-4a-private-defence`

§ `Chapter 16 -- Hurt`

-- Penal Code 1871 ss 319, 320, 321, 322, 324, 326, 327, 328, 329, 330, 331, 332,
-- 333, 334, 334A, 335, 335A, 335B, 336, 337, 338.
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/PC1871.txt.
--
-- This is the definitional core of Chapter 16, and the reason it was encoded first:
-- "an offence affecting the human body" in s 97(a) is what the right of private
-- defence defends against, and until this module existed Chapter 4A could decide
-- that an act was justified with no offence to report the justification against.
--
-- Shape of the group. ss 319 and 320 define hurt and grievous hurt. ss 321 and 322
-- add the fault element that makes the causing "voluntary". Everything from s 324 on
-- is that voluntary causing plus one aggravating circumstance -- a dangerous means,
-- a purpose, a victim, or a provocation -- and the aggravated sections come in pairs,
-- one for hurt and one for grievous hurt. ss 335B to 338 are a separate family that
-- turns on rashness or negligence rather than on intention or knowledge.
--
-- PUNISHMENT IS NOT COMPUTED. ss 323, 323A, 325, 334A and 336 are punishment
-- provisions and several sections open "except in the case provided for by section
-- X", which allocates which punishment section applies rather than whether the
-- conduct is an offence. Those carve-outs are recorded in the comments and are not
-- encoded as elements. s 323A and s 334A are encoded anyway, because each states a
-- distinct combination of fault and result that a caller may want to test.

§§ `Section 319 -- Hurt`

-- Whoever causes bodily pain, disease or infirmity to any person is said to cause
-- hurt. Explanation: a person is said to cause hurt if he causes another person to
-- be unconscious.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 319"
@export Decide whether hurt is caused within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 319
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc Bodily pain, disease or infirmity caused to any person, or causing another person to be unconscious.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `hurt is caused` IF
        h's `causes bodily pain to any person`
    OR  h's `causes disease to any person`
    OR  h's `causes infirmity to any person`
    OR  h's `causes another person to be unconscious`

§§ `Section 320 -- Grievous hurt`

-- "The following kinds of hurt only are designated as grievous" -- ten of them,
-- (a), (aa) and (b) to (i). The word "only" is why this is a closed list and why
-- the rule is a bare disjunction with no residual limb.
--
-- Grievous hurt is a kind of hurt, so s 319 must also be satisfied. The Act does not
-- say so in terms, but every limb of s 320 describes a hurt, and s 322 speaks of
-- "the hurt which he causes" being grievous hurt. Limb (aa), death, is the one that
-- makes this worth stating: death is grievous hurt for Chapter 16 purposes.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 320"
@export Decide whether the hurt is grievous hurt within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 320
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc The hurt caused, and which of the ten kinds in s 320(a) to (i) it is. s 319 must also be satisfied.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `grievous hurt is caused` IF
        `hurt is caused` h
    AND (   h's `the hurt is emasculation`
         OR h's `the hurt is death`
         OR h's `the hurt is permanent privation of the sight of either eye`
         OR h's `the hurt is permanent privation of the hearing of either ear`
         OR h's `the hurt is privation of any member or joint`
         OR h's `the hurt is destruction or permanent impairing of the powers of any member or joint`
         OR h's `the hurt is permanent disfiguration of the head or face`
         OR h's `the hurt is fracture or dislocation of a bone`
         OR h's `the hurt endangers life or causes the sufferer to be during the space of 20 days in severe bodily pain or unable to follow his ordinary pursuits`
         OR h's `the hurt is penetration of the vagina or anus of a person without that person consent which causes severe bodily pain`)

§§ `Section 321 -- Voluntarily causing hurt`

-- Whoever does any act with the intention of thereby causing hurt to any person, or
-- with the knowledge that he is likely thereby to cause hurt to any person, and does
-- thereby cause hurt to any person, is said voluntarily to cause hurt.
--
-- Three elements: the fault (intention or knowledge), and the result (hurt in fact).
-- Note that the person intended and the person hurt need not be the same -- the
-- section says "to any person" in both places.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 321"
@export Decide whether hurt is voluntarily caused within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 321
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc The fault element -- intention to cause hurt, or knowledge that hurt is likely -- together with hurt actually caused.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `hurt is voluntarily caused` IF
        (   h's `does the act with the intention of thereby causing hurt to any person`
         OR h's `does the act with the knowledge that he is likely thereby to cause hurt to any person`)
    AND `hurt is caused` h

§§ `Section 322 -- Voluntarily causing grievous hurt`

-- Whoever voluntarily causes hurt, if the hurt which he intends to cause or knows
-- himself to be likely to cause is grievous hurt, and if the hurt which he causes is
-- grievous hurt, is said voluntarily to cause grievous hurt.
--
-- The Explanation states both halves: a person is not said voluntarily to cause
-- grievous hurt except when he BOTH causes grievous hurt AND intends or knows
-- himself likely to cause grievous hurt -- but he is so said if, intending grievous
-- hurt of one kind, he actually causes grievous hurt of another kind. The second
-- half is why the rule does not require the intended kind and the caused kind to
-- match: `the hurt intended or known to be likely is grievous hurt` is a single
-- fact about gravity, not about which limb of s 320.
-- Illustration: intending permanent disfiguration but in fact causing 20 days of
-- severe bodily pain is voluntarily causing grievous hurt.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 322"
@export Decide whether grievous hurt is voluntarily caused within the meaning of Penal Code 1871 section 322
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc Voluntary causing of hurt, where the hurt intended or known to be likely is grievous and the hurt actually caused is grievous. The two kinds need not match.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `grievous hurt is voluntarily caused` IF
        `hurt is voluntarily caused` h
    AND h's `the hurt intended or known to be likely is grievous hurt`
    AND `grievous hurt is caused` h

§§ `Section 323A -- Voluntarily causing hurt which causes grievous hurt`

-- s 323A is a punishment section, but the combination it describes is distinct and
-- worth testing: the hurt intended or known to be likely is NOT grievous, but the
-- hurt actually caused is. It sits between s 321 and s 322.
-- Illustration: a punch intended to cause minor facial injury, where the victim
-- falls, strikes his head and is permanently paralysed.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 323A"
@export Decide whether the case is one of voluntarily causing hurt which causes grievous hurt under Penal Code 1871 section 323A
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc Voluntary causing of hurt where the hurt intended or known to be likely is not grievous but the hurt actually caused is grievous.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `hurt is voluntarily caused which causes grievous hurt` IF
        `hurt is voluntarily caused` h
    AND (NOT h's `the hurt intended or known to be likely is grievous hurt`)
    AND `grievous hurt is caused` h

§§ `Sections 324 and 326 -- Dangerous weapons or means`

-- The list of means is identical in both sections: any instrument for shooting,
-- stabbing or cutting; any instrument which, used as a weapon of offence, is likely
-- to cause death; fire or any heated substance; any poison or corrosive substance;
-- any explosive substance; any substance harmful to the human body to inhale,
-- swallow or receive into the blood; or any animal.
--
-- s 324 opens "except in the case provided for by section 334" and s 326 "except in
-- the case provided for by section 335". Both carve-outs allocate punishment between
-- the aggravated section and the provocation section; neither bears on whether the
-- conduct is within the section. They are not encoded as elements.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 324 and 326"
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hurt is caused by a dangerous weapon or means` IF
        h's `by means of any instrument for shooting stabbing or cutting`
    OR  h's `by means of any instrument which used as a weapon of offence is likely to cause death`
    OR  h's `by means of fire or any heated substance`
    OR  h's `by means of any poison or any corrosive substance`
    OR  h's `by means of any explosive substance`
    OR  h's `by means of any substance which it is harmful to the human body to inhale to swallow or to receive into the blood`
    OR  h's `by means of any animal`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 324"
@export Decide whether hurt is voluntarily caused by dangerous weapons or means under Penal Code 1871 section 324
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc Voluntary causing of hurt by one of the seven means listed in s 324.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes voluntarily causing hurt by dangerous weapons or means` IF
        `hurt is voluntarily caused` h
    AND `the hurt is caused by a dangerous weapon or means` h

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 326"
@export Decide whether grievous hurt is voluntarily caused by dangerous weapons or means under Penal Code 1871 section 326
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc Voluntary causing of grievous hurt by one of the seven means listed in s 326.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes voluntarily causing grievous hurt by dangerous weapons or means` IF
        `grievous hurt is voluntarily caused` h
    AND `the hurt is caused by a dangerous weapon or means` h

§§ `Sections 327 and 329 -- To extort property or to constrain to an illegal act`

-- Hurt (s 327) or grievous hurt (s 329) voluntarily caused for the purpose of
-- extorting from the sufferer, or any person interested in the sufferer, any
-- property or valuable security; or of constraining the sufferer or such a person to
-- do anything which is illegal or which may facilitate the commission of an offence.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 327 and 329"
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose is extorting property or constraining to an illegal act` IF
        h's `for the purpose of extorting from the sufferer or from any person interested in the sufferer any property or valuable security`
    OR  h's `for the purpose of constraining the sufferer or any person interested in the sufferer to do anything which is illegal or which may facilitate the commission of an offence`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 327"
@export Decide whether hurt is voluntarily caused to extort property or to constrain to an illegal act under Penal Code 1871 section 327
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc Voluntary causing of hurt for one of the two purposes in s 327.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes voluntarily causing hurt to extort property or constrain to an illegal act` IF
        `hurt is voluntarily caused` h
    AND `the purpose is extorting property or constraining to an illegal act` h

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 329"
@export Decide whether grievous hurt is voluntarily caused to extort property or to constrain to an illegal act under Penal Code 1871 section 329
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc Voluntary causing of grievous hurt for one of the two purposes in s 329.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes voluntarily causing grievous hurt to extort property or constrain to an illegal act` IF
        `grievous hurt is voluntarily caused` h
    AND `the purpose is extorting property or constraining to an illegal act` h

§§ `Section 328 -- Causing hurt by poison etc. with intent to commit an offence`

-- Whoever administers to, or causes to be taken by, any person any poison or any
-- stupefying or intoxicating substance, or any substance harmful to the human body
-- to inhale, swallow or receive into the blood, with intent to cause hurt to such
-- person, or with intent to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence, or
-- knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause hurt.
--
-- s 328 is the one section in this group that does NOT require hurt in fact. Its
-- elements are the administering and one of three fault states; the offence is
-- complete on administering with that intent or knowledge, whether or not hurt
-- follows. So it does not build on s 321.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 328"
@export Decide whether the act constitutes causing hurt by poison or other substance with intent under Penal Code 1871 section 328
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc Administering or causing to be taken a poison, stupefying or intoxicating substance, or a substance harmful to inhale, swallow or receive into the blood, with intent to cause hurt, or to commit or facilitate an offence, or knowing hurt is likely. Hurt in fact is not required.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes causing hurt by poison with intent to commit an offence` IF
        h's `administers to or causes to be taken by any person any poison or any stupefying or intoxicating substance or any substance which is harmful to the human body to inhale swallow or receive into the blood`
    AND (   h's `with intent to cause hurt to such person`
         OR h's `with intent to commit or to facilitate the commission of an offence`
         OR h's `knowing it to be likely that he will thereby cause hurt`)

§§ `Sections 330 and 331 -- To extort a confession or to compel restoration of property`

-- Hurt (s 330) or grievous hurt (s 331) voluntarily caused for the purpose of
-- extorting from the sufferer, or any person interested in the sufferer, any
-- confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or
-- misconduct; or of constraining such a person to restore or cause the restoration
-- of any property or valuable security, to satisfy any claim or demand, or to give
-- information which may lead to such restoration.
-- Illustrations (a) to (c) to s 330 are all police or customs officers torturing a
-- person to obtain a confession or the location of stolen property.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 330 and 331"
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the purpose is extorting a confession or compelling restoration` IF
        h's `for the purpose of extorting from the sufferer or from any person interested in the sufferer any confession or any information which may lead to the detection of an offence or misconduct`
    OR  h's `for the purpose of constraining the sufferer or any person interested in the sufferer to restore or to cause the restoration of any property or valuable security or to satisfy any claim or demand or to give information which may lead to such restoration`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 330"
@export Decide whether hurt is voluntarily caused to extort a confession or compel restoration of property under Penal Code 1871 section 330
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc Voluntary causing of hurt for one of the two purposes in s 330.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes voluntarily causing hurt to extort a confession` IF
        `hurt is voluntarily caused` h
    AND `the purpose is extorting a confession or compelling restoration` h

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 331"
@export Decide whether grievous hurt is voluntarily caused to extort a confession or compel restoration of property under Penal Code 1871 section 331
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc Voluntary causing of grievous hurt for one of the two purposes in s 331.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes voluntarily causing grievous hurt to extort a confession` IF
        `grievous hurt is voluntarily caused` h
    AND `the purpose is extorting a confession or compelling restoration` h

§§ `Sections 332 and 333 -- To deter a public servant from his duty`

-- Hurt (s 332) or grievous hurt (s 333) voluntarily caused to a person being a
-- public servant in the discharge of his duty as such; or with intent to prevent or
-- deter that person or any other public servant from discharging his duty as such;
-- or in consequence of anything done or attempted to be done by that person in the
-- lawful discharge of his duty as such.
--
-- The three limbs are alternatives, and only the first is about the victim's status
-- at the moment of the hurt. The proviso to s 332 -- that in exceptional
-- circumstances imprisonment need not be imposed -- is a sentencing direction and is
-- not encoded.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 332 and 333"
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the hurt is to a public servant or to deter one from his duty` IF
        h's `the person hurt is a public servant in the discharge of his duty as such public servant`
    OR  h's `with intent to prevent or deter that person or any other public servant from discharging his duty as such public servant`
    OR  h's `in consequence of anything done or attempted to be done by that person in the lawful discharge of his duty as such public servant`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 332"
@export Decide whether hurt is voluntarily caused to deter a public servant from his duty under Penal Code 1871 section 332
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc Voluntary causing of hurt on one of the three public-servant limbs of s 332.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes voluntarily causing hurt to deter a public servant` IF
        `hurt is voluntarily caused` h
    AND `the hurt is to a public servant or to deter one from his duty` h

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 333"
@export Decide whether grievous hurt is voluntarily caused to deter a public servant from his duty under Penal Code 1871 section 333
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc Voluntary causing of grievous hurt on one of the three public-servant limbs of s 333.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes voluntarily causing grievous hurt to deter a public servant` IF
        `grievous hurt is voluntarily caused` h
    AND `the hurt is to a public servant or to deter one from his duty` h

§§ `Sections 334, 334A and 335 -- On grave and sudden provocation`

-- s 334: voluntarily causing hurt on grave and sudden provocation, if the accused
-- neither intends nor knows himself likely to cause hurt to any person other than
-- the person who gave the provocation.
-- s 334A: the same, where the hurt intended or known to be likely is not grievous
-- but the hurt actually caused is.
-- s 335: voluntarily causing grievous hurt on grave and sudden provocation, if he
-- neither intends nor knows himself likely to cause grievous hurt to any person
-- other than the person who gave the provocation. Note the confinement limb is about
-- grievous hurt in s 335 where it is about hurt in ss 334 and 334A.
--
-- Explanation: ss 334, 334A and 335 are subject to the same provisos as Exception 1
-- to s 300. Those provisos are in the culpable homicide group and are not encoded
-- here; a caller testing a provocation section should read them with it.
-- These three reduce liability rather than create it -- they are the mitigated
-- counterparts of ss 321, 323A and 322 -- so each is a test on the same facts plus
-- the provocation limbs, not an offence that stands alone.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 334"
@export Decide whether hurt is voluntarily caused on grave and sudden provocation under Penal Code 1871 section 334
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc Voluntary causing of hurt on grave and sudden provocation, with no intention or knowledge of hurt to anyone other than the provoker.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes voluntarily causing hurt on provocation` IF
        `hurt is voluntarily caused` h
    AND h's `the hurt is caused on grave and sudden provocation`
    AND h's `neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 334A"
@export Decide whether the case is one of voluntarily causing hurt on provocation which causes grievous hurt under Penal Code 1871 section 334A
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc As s 334, where the hurt intended or known to be likely is not grievous but the hurt actually caused is grievous.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes voluntarily causing hurt on provocation which causes grievous hurt` IF
        `constitutes voluntarily causing hurt on provocation` h
    AND (NOT h's `the hurt intended or known to be likely is grievous hurt`)
    AND `grievous hurt is caused` h

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 335"
@export Decide whether grievous hurt is caused on grave and sudden provocation under Penal Code 1871 section 335
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc Voluntary causing of grievous hurt on grave and sudden provocation, with no intention or knowledge of grievous hurt to anyone other than the provoker.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes causing grievous hurt on provocation` IF
        `grievous hurt is voluntarily caused` h
    AND h's `the hurt is caused on grave and sudden provocation`
    AND h's `neither intends nor knows himself to be likely to cause grievous hurt to any person other than the person who gave the provocation`

§§ `Section 335A -- Allowing neglect or abuse of a domestic worker or vulnerable person`

-- s 335A(1) (domestic worker) and s 335A(2) (vulnerable person) have the same five
-- paragraphs and differ only in paragraph (c): for a domestic worker the accused
-- must have been the employer, a member of the employer's household or an employment
-- agent; for a vulnerable person the accused must have had custody, charge or care.
--
-- s 335A(3) defines the "unlawful act" of the third party C. It is an act
-- constituting an offence causing that neglect, hurt, grievous hurt, sexual abuse or
-- injury to mental health, OR one that would constitute such an offence but for C
-- being below the s 82 age, within s 83 without sufficient maturity, or entitled to
-- rely on unsoundness of mind, intoxication or mistake of fact. The five exculpated
-- cases are gathered into one caller-asserted fact rather than expanded, because
-- each of them is itself a Chapter 4 test already encoded in
-- `chapter-4-exceptions.l4` and applying it here would require the third party's own
-- facts, which this record does not carry.
--
-- s 335A(4) provides that the accused's circumstances include past or present
-- experience of suffering the same treatment at the hands of C. That widens what a
-- court may consider under paragraph (d); it adds no limb and is not encoded.
-- s 335A(5) is punishment, and s 335A(6) definitions, drawing "domestic worker" from
-- s 73(4), "neglect" from s 304B(2) and "vulnerable person" from s 74A(5). Those
-- cross-references are carried as caller-asserted status facts.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 335A(3)"
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the third party act is an unlawful act within section 335A(3)` IF
        h's `the act of that other person constitutes an offence causing that neglect hurt grievous hurt sexual abuse or injury`
    OR  h's `the act of that other person would constitute such an offence but for his being within section 82 or section 83 or entitled to rely on unsoundness of mind intoxication or mistake of fact`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 335A(1) and (2)"
@export Decide whether the accused is guilty of allowing neglect or abuse of a domestic worker or vulnerable person under Penal Code 1871 section 335A
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc The victim's status as a domestic worker or vulnerable person, the suffering caused by a third party's unlawful act, the accused's knowledge of the risk, the accused's relationship to the victim, the failure to take reasonable protective steps, and foreseeability of the circumstances.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes allowing neglect or abuse of a domestic worker or vulnerable person` IF
        h's `the victim suffers neglect hurt grievous hurt sexual abuse or any injury to mental health as a result of the unlawful act of another person`
    AND `the third party act is an unlawful act within section 335A(3)` h
    AND h's `the accused knew or had reason to believe that the victim was at risk of such neglect hurt grievous hurt sexual abuse or injury caused by that other person`
    AND (   (    h's `the victim is a domestic worker within section 73(4)`
             AND h's `the accused was at the time of the risk the employer of the victim a member of the employer household or an employment agent of the victim`)
         OR (    h's `the victim is a vulnerable person within section 74A(5)`
             AND h's `the accused had at the time of the risk the custody charge or care of the victim`))
    AND h's `the accused failed to take such steps as could reasonably have been expected in the accused circumstances to protect the victim from that risk`
    AND h's `the act occurred in circumstances of the kind that the accused foresaw or ought to have foreseen`

§§ `Sections 335B to 338 -- Acts endangering life or the personal safety of others`

-- s 335B: doing an act that endangers human life or the personal safety of others,
-- knowing or believing that the act is likely to cause death.
-- s 336: doing an act so rashly or negligently as to endanger human life or the
-- personal safety of others. Punishment differs between the rash and the negligent
-- case, which is why the two are separate facts and not one.
-- s 337: the same rash or negligent act, where hurt is caused.
-- s 338: the same, where grievous hurt is caused.
--
-- This family does not build on s 321. Its fault element is knowledge or belief
-- (s 335B) or rashness or negligence (ss 336 to 338), not the intention or knowledge
-- of hurt that s 321 requires, and ss 335B and 336 require no hurt at all.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 336"
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act is rash or negligent and endangers life or personal safety` IF
        h's `does the act so rashly as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others`
    OR  h's `does the act so negligently as to endanger human life or the personal safety of others`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 335B"
@export Decide whether the act endangers life or personal safety with knowledge or belief that it is likely to cause death under Penal Code 1871 section 335B
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc An act endangering human life or the personal safety of others, done knowing or believing it likely to cause death. No hurt in fact is required.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes an act endangering life with knowledge that death is likely` IF
        h's `does an act that endangers human life or the personal safety of others`
    AND h's `knowing or believing that such act is likely to cause death`

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 336"
@export Decide whether the act rashly or negligently endangers life or the personal safety of others under Penal Code 1871 section 336
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc A rash or negligent act endangering human life or the personal safety of others. No hurt in fact is required.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes an act endangering life or personal safety` IF
    `the act is rash or negligent and endangers life or personal safety` h

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 337"
@export Decide whether hurt is caused by an act endangering life or the personal safety of others under Penal Code 1871 section 337
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc A rash or negligent act endangering human life or the personal safety of others, by which hurt is caused.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes causing hurt by an act endangering life` IF
        `the act is rash or negligent and endangers life or personal safety` h
    AND `hurt is caused` h

@ref "Penal Code 1871, s 338"
@export Decide whether grievous hurt is caused by an act endangering life or the personal safety of others under Penal Code 1871 section 338
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc A rash or negligent act endangering human life or the personal safety of others, by which grievous hurt is caused.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `constitutes causing grievous hurt by an act endangering life` IF
        `the act is rash or negligent and endangers life or personal safety` h
    AND `grievous hurt is caused` h

§§ `An offence affecting the human body`

-- s 97(a) gives a right of private defence of the body "against any offence
-- affecting the human body". Chapter 16 is the Chapter of those offences, and this
-- predicate is what the encoded part of it now supplies: TRUE where any offence in
-- this module is made out on the facts.
--
-- It is deliberately NOT wired into `there is a section 97(a) right to defend the
-- body`, which continues to take the offence element as a caller-asserted fact. Two
-- reasons. The facts that would have to be asserted are the assailant's, not the
-- defender's, and the `Proposed Act` bundle carries one actor's facts only. And this
-- module is one group of seven in Chapter 16, so a FALSE here is not yet a statement
-- that no offence affecting the human body is in play. Wiring it in would make the
-- private-defence right look computed when it is not.

@ref "Penal Code 1871, ss 321, 322, 328, 335A, 335B, 336"
@export Decide whether any Penal Code 1871 hurt offence encoded here is made out on the facts
GIVEN h IS A `Bodily Harm` @desc The bodily-harm facts. Returns TRUE if any of ss 321, 322, 324, 326, 327, 328, 329, 330, 331, 332, 333, 335A, 335B, 336, 337 or 338 is made out.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an encoded hurt offence is made out` IF
        `hurt is voluntarily caused` h
    OR  `grievous hurt is voluntarily caused` h
    OR  `constitutes causing hurt by poison with intent to commit an offence` h
    OR  `constitutes allowing neglect or abuse of a domestic worker or vulnerable person` h
    OR  `constitutes an act endangering life with knowledge that death is likely` h
    OR  `constitutes an act endangering life or personal safety` h

§§ `Proposed Act wrappers`

-- As everywhere in this encoding, the wrapper applies s 6: a Chapter 4 general
-- exception or a Chapter 4A private defence takes the act outside the offence.
-- Private defence matters here more than anywhere else in the subject -- these are
-- the offences it is most often raised against.

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes voluntarily causing hurt` IF
        `hurt is voluntarily caused` (a's `bodily harm`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes voluntarily causing grievous hurt` IF
        `grievous hurt is voluntarily caused` (a's `bodily harm`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes causing hurt by poison` IF
        `constitutes causing hurt by poison with intent to commit an offence` (a's `bodily harm`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes allowing neglect or abuse` IF
        `constitutes allowing neglect or abuse of a domestic worker or vulnerable person` (a's `bodily harm`)
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)

GIVEN a IS A `Proposed Act`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the proposed act constitutes an act endangering life or personal safety` IF
        (   `constitutes an act endangering life with knowledge that death is likely` (a's `bodily harm`)
         OR `constitutes an act endangering life or personal safety` (a's `bodily harm`))
    AND NOT (`the act is taken outside offence by Chapter 4 or Chapter 4A` a)
